# Runs that recorded a silent CPU fallback rather than GPU execution: kept on
# disk for reference, never committed - the numbers do not measure what the
# harness claims to measure.
*/invalid-*/
# Figure previews; the committed figure is the vector PDF beside them.
*/*/figures/*.png
*/*/figures/*.svg
# run_models.sh's argmax scratch: one file per system, written and re-read
# inside a single stage and deleted when it ends. Never a result.
*/*/.last_argmax_*

# Row data is committed packed, one data.tar.gz per run: about 3MB of tsv and
# jsonl becomes 300KB, and results.jsonl stops rewriting itself whole in the
# history on every stage. benchmark/paper/archive.sh packs and unpacks it;
# machine.txt, summary.md and figures/ stay loose so a run can be read
# without downloading anything.
*/*/*.tsv
*/*/results.jsonl
*/*/.warmup_series/
# The MOTION leave check's per-run files (packed, see archive.sh), the warm
# kernel cache run_motion.sh keeps for its sweeps, and run_decode.sh's token
# scratch.
*/*/leave/
*/*/.motion_cache/
*/*/.decode_tokens_*
